-- title:
--   Option Basis Proj Sum Eq One
-- statement:
--   **The auxiliary Option basis projectors resolve the identity.** For a finite outcome type `alpha`, associate to every `oa : Option alpha` the rank-one matrix projector onto the corresponding auxiliary basis vector. Summing all these projectors, including the distinguished `none` failure vector, gives the identity operator on the auxiliary space:
--
--   $$
--   \sum_{oa\in\operatorname{Option}(\alpha)} |oa\rangle\!\langle oa|=I_{\operatorname{Option}(\alpha)}.
--   $$
--
--   This finite resolution of identity is the normalization fact that makes the Naimark outcome projectors complete after adding the auxiliary failure outcome.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.MakingMeasurementsProjective.optionBasisProj_sum_eq_one`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
